# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# --- Project-specific: market data artifacts ---
# Raw captures and reconstructed output are large, binary, and regenerable
# from capture.py/reconstruct.py -- they do not belong in git (this mirrors
# capture.py's own "capture is the irreplaceable asset, but it's also huge"
# framing: keep the *code* that produces it in version control, not the
# multi-GB output itself).
*.jsonl.zst
*.parquet
capture_data/
capture_out/
reconstruction_out/
smoke_capture*/
smoke_e2e*/

# Scratch/debug scripts this session used during development (prefixed
# with an underscore by convention) -- never meant to be committed.
_smoke_*.py
_debug_*.py
